import MassGap.Fluctuation  -- the fluctuation-dissipation identity on a FINITE Gibbs family, and the derivative bound the interior grid asks for. gibbs_mean_deriv_eq_neg_cov proves d<A>/dbeta = -Cov(A,E) by the quotient rule on Z and the weighted sum -- the general form of gibbs_susceptibility_eq_variance, whose A = E case makes the susceptibility a VARIANCE and so nonnegative with no physics input. That identity is also what WilsonAnalytic proves for the Haar integral; here it is the finite sum, which is the setting in which the two steps the A1-uniform plan names and never formalises are elementary: abs_Covf_le_sqrt_mul_sqrt is Cauchy-Schwarz on the half-weights exp(-beta E_i/2) (the centred sums are Z*Cov, Z*Var A and Z*Var E, so the common Z^2 divides out), and VarObs_le_sq_range_div_four is Popoviciu from the observable's range alone. Composed, norm_deriv_meanf_le bounds ||d<A>/dbeta|| by a quarter of the product of the two ranges -- a CONSTANT, and one derived rather than measured or assumed -- and norm_deriv_meanf_le_on states it in the exact shape of Interior.d2_le_of_analytic_grid's hbnd, with differentiableAt_meanf_on meeting its hdiff and meanf_lipschitz meeting le_of_lipschitz_grid's hlip. What it does NOT do is instantiate at Interior.d2: that is Complete.d2At, a read built from the opaque wilsonCorrAt whose beta-dependence nothing relates to a finite Gibbs weight, and the Wilson ensemble's own measure is a Haar integral. So this supplies hbnd's shape and its constant at FIXED volume; the volume-uniform B that confinement_of_bounded_substrate needs is untouched and remains clustering. No axiom.
import MassGap.Majorization  -- the deterministic form of the disorder-susceptibility sign, with no probability in it. PAPER 8.4's chi_v = -dH/dbeta >= 0 is the one input the interior route cannot measure; stated about the SPECTRUM rather than the coupling it becomes a monotonicity along the straight segment p(s) = (1-s)r + s q, and entropy_antitone proves the Shannon entropy non-increasing there under one scalar start condition, 0 <= sum_k (q_k - r_k) log r_k. The whole content is termwise: (q_k - r_k)(log p_k(s) - log r_k) = r_k x_k log(1 + s x_k) >= 0, so the derivative never exceeds its value at s = 0. The point of the file is that the start condition is not an extra assumption where it matters. concentration_at_dominant discharges it outright for a point-mass limit q = e_j at r's heaviest component, since the sum is then sum_k r_k log(r_j/r_k), a divergence; concentration_of_majorizes discharges it for ANY aligned q that majorizes r, by summation-by-parts into sum_m D_m (log r_{m-1} - log r_m) with both factors nonnegative. So entropy_antitone_at_dominant and entropy_antitone_of_majorizes are unconditional, which is the Schur-concavity of entropy in the one direction the argument uses. No axiom, no reflection positivity, no transfer matrix.
import MassGap.ShareEnvelope  -- why the unnormalised route must NOT carry a mass floor, and what a doubling condition does and does not buy. scaleRead exhibits the read rescaled by t, which is why a uniform mass floor c <= sum rho cannot survive: the SHARE is scale-invariant while the mass is not, so any bound stated on the unnormalised correlation is refuted by rescaling alone -- and that is exactly what fails as beta grows, since links approach the identity and the plaquette variance vanishes. farShare_doubling_iff_tail_mass restates a doubling condition as a tail-mass one, substrate_of_tail_mass_doubling feeds it to the criterion, and readYMAt_rho records that the Wilson read's weights ARE the constructed correlation, by rfl. The negative controls are the content: doubling_load_bearing and quarter_doubling_is_not_enough / quarter_doubling_gives_no_bound show a quarter-rate doubling condition does NOT bound the moment, via squareRead's exact telescoping tail mass -- so the doubling route needs a rate strictly better than a quarter, and mass_floor_is_not_scale_free names the scale-invariance that kills the unnormalised form. Foundational only except where readYMAt enters.
import MassGap.OddLagSplit  -- the odd-lag geometry, algebra and reduction, and the obstruction LIFTED to the sum. cfgSum puts gNeg on every reflection-fixed axis link whose site has EVEN coordinate sum, and sum_val_shift_parity is why that works: at EVEN extent a transverse step FLIPS the coordinate-sum parity (unwrapped it adds one; wrapped it drops n-1 to 0, and n-1 is odd), so of the two fixed axis links a straddling plaquette reads, exactly ONE has even sum -- making every straddling plaquette read -1 at once where cfgWitness moved only one. straddling_sum_not_paired_at_odd_lag and no_half_function_for_straddling_sum lift both refutations to the exponential-of-a-sum, which was the scoped gap. oplaq_side partitions every non-degenerate plaquette into one half ALONE (sharper than the even case, where a one-sided plaquette reads its half plus the plane) or the OddCross class the refutation defeats. hsRe_dsum_conj is hsRe_conj for a whole family with EACH BLOCK conjugated by its own gauge pair, which is what the lattice supplies since every straddling plaquette carries its own two fixed axis links. corrClay_rp_of_odd_lags then reduces the whole axiom at any EVEN extent to ONE hypothesis, PlaqReflPositive at the odd lags: the even lags come from ActionSplit.plaqReflPositive_of_even_lag and lag zero from PlaqVariance.corrClay_zero_pos, neither assumed. NEW BLOCKER, named here for the first time: cross_word_both_handednesses shows a link reflection has TWO fixed planes presenting the gauge with OPPOSITE handedness -- at level 0 the positive half owns one transverse link and the gauge acts as F -> g F h-inverse, at level m it owns the other and the same word reads F -> g-inverse F h. On a non-abelian group those compose in opposite orders and are not one action, which is what wilson_crossing_pairing_nonneg requires. Repairable by inverting one plane's variables under the integral (isInvInvariant_probHaar licenses it); not yet done. Foundational only.
import MassGap.CrossingIntegration  -- the odd-lag crossing integration, done with NO representation theory -- and the cheap finish REFUTED first. straddling_word_not_matrix_paired_at_odd_lag and no_half_function_for_straddling_word prove, two independent ways, that the straddling word G F G'-inverse (Theta F)-inverse is NOT X (Theta X)-dagger and is not any function of the two half-restrictions: a paired form is a SQUARE at a reflection-fixed configuration, and cfgWitness -- the identity everywhere except one reflection-FIXED axis link carrying diag(1,-1,-1), which is its own inverse and is why the configuration is fixed -- makes the straddling word read Re tr = -1. The second obstruction is stronger: a fixed axis link lies in NEITHER half, so moving it moves the word and leaves both half-restrictions untouched, which refutes every candidate including rescalings and additive constants. THE POSITIVE RESULT: the plane links act on the transverse links exactly as a GAUGE FIELD acts on link variables, so the straddling word IS the same cross form the Wilson weight already has with the plane links absorbed into one argument. hsRe_conj says the cross form does not see the plane gauge (cyclicity of the trace), wilson_kernel_integral_psd says the weight is a positive-semidefinite kernel against any probability measure, and crossing_gauge_integral_eq moves the plane average onto BOTH factors of the pairing -- which is the job Schur orthogonality does in Osterwalder-Seiler, done without it. The moment route was checked and is the expensive one: exp(beta Re tr W)'s order-k term is degree k in the plane-link coordinates, so it needs BALANCED moments at every order, and HaarMoments is exact for SU(2) only through order 3 and brackets the balanced fourth in [1/4, 1/2]; truncating at the second moment is 6.5 percent off at beta = 1 and is a strong-coupling expansion of the weight, not the weight. SCOPE, stated because it was overreached in a first draft: both obstructions are about ONE straddling plaquette, and the Boltzmann weight's straddling factor is the exponential of a SUM -- the sum-level claim is NOT proved. And wilson_crossing_pairing_nonneg is over an abstract Omega, Gamma, X; nothing ties X to wilsonHol. What remains for odd lags is the action split, lattice bookkeeping of the kind ActionSplit does for even lags, with no representation theory in it.
import MassGap.ContactDominance  -- THE ONE REMAINING HYPOTHESIS, reformulated sharply. circ_moment_eq_layer is an IDENTITY, not a bound: because k^2 = sum over m<k of (2m+1), the circle second moment IS the (2m+1)-weighted profile of the far-share beyond each cut. So the flagship's hypothesis is EXACTLY a uniform bound on that profile. substrate_of_share_envelope and yang_mills_of_share_envelope take any summable envelope a with sum (2m+1) a m finite and deliver the full gap/non-triviality/SO(4) conjunct, with B the envelope's own weighted total -- no constant introduced. THE THRESHOLD EXPONENT IS EXACTLY 2, PROVED BOTH WAYS: substrate_of_cubic_share works above it, square_envelope_not_summable shows the criterion cannot be entered at it, and square_share_is_not_enough shows the STATEMENT IS FALSE at it -- squareRead satisfies exactly the two clauses the RP axiom asserts, has far-share at most 1/(m+1)^2, and its moment dominates the harmonic series. Controls: contactRead gives a nonvacuous envelope at zero, antipodeRead forces a == 1 whose weighted sum diverges, so summability is load-bearing rather than decorative. Route (a) is CLOSED with arithmetic: substrateThreshold_lt_ceiling proves the forward run of substrate_lt_of_tension_lt_floor outputs 0.030020 while confinement_at_of_substrate_sharp consumes 0.012716, short by exactly pi^2/4 = 2.4674, which is the loss cos_le_one_sub_mul_cos_sq takes against Sharp.cos_ge_tangent. Route (b) is downstream not upstream: WilsonAnalytic's only volume-free covariance bound CONSUMES clustering of the connected correlator, and its unconditional one is extensive. CAVEAT worth heeding: the unnormalised envelope-plus-mass form is a TRAP, because the uniform mass bound is almost certainly false as beta grows -- links go to the identity and the plaquette variance vanishes -- which is exactly why StrongCoupling.read_p_le_of_corrClay's per-N mass hypotheses are unproved. The SHARE form is the one that survives.
import MassGap.CharacterExpansion  -- the SU(N) Wilson weight is POSITIVE-DEFINITE at physical coupling, and two mechanism gaps closed. wilson_kernel_nonneg: exp(beta * Re tr(A B-dagger)) is a positive-definite kernel for beta >= 0, proved with no representation theory -- Re tr(A B-dagger) is the Euclidean inner product on the 2N^2 real coordinates, so every power splits into PAIRED monomials with no cross terms and the coefficients are multiplicities written out as a monomial index. NEGATIVE CONTROL as an IFF: two genuine SU(3) elements and weights (1,-1) give 2(exp(3 beta) - exp(-beta)), nonnegative exactly when 0 <= beta, so the hypothesis is load-bearing and is seen to block. NOT formalised, and the docstring says so: the Peter-Weyl dictionary. Nothing here uses it, so irreducible characters are never named -- do not read these as SU(3) character theory in Lean. Two gaps closed: twisted_reflection_positive_of_expansion points the tree's expansion mechanism at the ACTUAL reflection (reflection_positive_of_expansion is stated for a bare relabelling U-compose-theta, while reflConf DAGGERS the axis links, so it was inapplicable), and crossweight_pairing_nonneg is the first statement in the tree admitting a term that genuinely COUPLES the two halves, where ActionSplit's weld requires every plaquette to read one side plus the plane. THE BLOCKER IS NOT THE COEFFICIENTS: odd_lag_straddling_plaq_two_fixed_axis_links proves the straddling plaquette word carries TWO distinct fixed axis links, both inverted by the reflection, so the word is G F G'-inverse (Theta F)-inverse and there is no paired word to expand -- the expansion has nothing to act on. What remains is the crossing-link Haar integration yielding a Gram matrix, i.e. Schur orthogonality / Peter-Weyl, which Mathlib does not supply for SU(3).
import MassGap.ActionSplit  -- the THREE-BLOCK weld, which was the tree's stated blocker on reflection positivity. ReflectionPositivity.pairing_with_reflection_nonneg needs Disjoint S T and integrates against bare product Haar, but under a reflection the links ON the plane are read by BOTH halves, so it never applied to the Wilson weight; WilsonReal.block_integral_factor was the only decomposition and is two-block plus disjoint. pairing_eq_weighted_square supplies the conditional form: the integral of W(U|R) * O * O(twist U) equals the integral of W(U|R) * (half-integral)^2, with the SHARED block outside the square, the OS dagger carried by twist, and a nonnegative plane weight riding along -- which is where exp(-beta S0) goes. NEGATIVE CONTROL, a theorem not a remark: on a fair coin the true pairing is 1/2 while the inside-the-square form gives 1/4, and shared_block_inside_square_false refutes the inside form outright, so the disjointness hypothesis of the old lemma was load-bearing. The reflection's parity structure is characterised: at EVEN extent with even constant the fixed set is transverse links only (no_fixed_axis_link) and is nonempty (exists_fixed_transverse_link), which is the covered case; at odd constant, and at every constant when the extent is ODD, a fixed AXIS link exists and reflConf INVERTS it (reflConf_inverts_fixed_axis_link), so the two factors are functions of u and of u-inverse and there is nothing to condition on. This does NOT discharge wilson_reflection_positive_at, not even partially: corrClay_rp_of needs PlaqReflPositive at every lag, and the remaining pieces are the plaquette partition in the favourable case and the genuine character expansion in the unfavourable one -- the latter being exactly what the proved reflection_positive_of_expansion is waiting to consume. Foundational only.
import MassGap.GibbsPositive  -- the reflected Schwinger form is NOWHERE zero, closing a pre-existing non-degeneracy gap: the clamp in QG meant nothing ruled out Q == 0, and a family with Q == 0 satisfies every OS field vacuously, so the continuum limit it produced would be the zero measure. corrNum_plaqObs_pos proves 0 < corrNum from continuity plus one configuration: probHaar is Haar hence IsOpenPosMeasure, Measure.pi carries that to configurations, so a continuous nonnegative integrand integrating to zero vanishes at EVERY configuration. 0 < partition was already in the tree (WilsonReal.wilsonSystem_partition_pos) and is reused, not re-proved. The gauge input is ONE group element: confD puts gD = diag(1,-1,-1) on the direction-0 links of one slice, the boundary word reads gD, density 4/3. ymFamilyGauge_Q_pos and ymFamilyGaugeCounted_Q_pos give 0 < Q for WilsonGauge.ymFamilyGauge and hence for WilsonModel.ymFamilyTension. WilsonInstance.ymFamily is a DIFFERENT form (QYM, not QG) and QYM_pos_of reduces it to 0 < wilsonCorrAt N a lag, which at lag 0 is exactly PlaqVariance.corrClay_zero_pos. NEGATIVE CONTROLS: the same machinery gives expect = 0 EXACTLY for the centred observable (so nonnegativity is load-bearing, not a formality) and for the same observable at SU(1) (so the group content is load-bearing). CAVEAT, and it is a real one: the spacing index enters this family AS THE COUPLING, so continuum_of_family's limit is beta -> infinity, the corrNum bound degrades like e^(-2 beta |Plaq|), and Q > 0 at every finite spacing does NOT give q != 0 in the limit. A lower bound uniform in beta, or a family whose spacing index is not the coupling, is still needed for a nonzero continuum measure.
import MassGap.PlaqVariance  -- the NON-RP half of wilson_reflection_positive_at, CLOSED. ReflectPositive.corrClay_rp_of reduces the axiom to two things of different provenance: textbook Osterwalder-Seiler, and 0 < corrClay (N+1) beta 0 -- which is positivity of the plaquette energy's VARIANCE and is not reflection positivity at all, since the identically-zero correlation satisfies every pairing inequality and fails it. corrClay_zero_pos proves it for ALL N and ALL real beta including zero and negative, foundational-only. At lag 0 the two plaquettes are literally the same plaquette (siteAtHyper tau 0 = fun _ => 0), so no displacement or translation invariance is needed. The mechanism is wilsonCorrConn_self_pos, stated for any SU(N) and any boundary word: product Haar over links is IsOpenPosMeasure, so Continuous.ae_eq_iff_eq turns a continuous nonnegative integrand integrating to zero into vanishing at EVERY configuration, which with the strictly positive Boltzmann weight forces the observable globally constant -- stronger than an a.e. statement and it skips Radon-Nikodym entirely. The gauge-group input is then ONE inequality: confOne gives phi = 0, confAB gives phi = 4/3 via a commutator of two real involutions in SU(3). NEGATIVE CONTROL: at SU(1) the group is trivial, su_one_has_no_two_values makes the hypothesis unsatisfiable, and wilsonCorrConn_self_eq_zero_of_trivial gives exactly 0 -- so the hypothesis is the whole gauge-group content, not decoration, and strictness was confirmed by deliberately breaking confAB to a commuting pair and watching the build fail at obs_confAB.
import MassGap.WilsonModel  -- THE ASSEMBLY. existence_and_gap_of_substrate and mass_gap_rate_and_continuum_of_substrate take ONE hypothesis -- exists B, forall N beta, d2At N beta <= B -- where the existing ymFullModelOf and ymFullModelGauge take four (hconf, hdom, hfe, hgap), and deliver the mass gap, non-triviality, SO(4) AND the OS0-OS3 continuum measure at EVERY beta with no half-line restriction. The joint that was missing is count_le_of_tension_uniform: ScreenedGap.resolvedDim_le_of_tension caps the resolved-mode count at ONE spacing by a bound carrying that spacing's own weight sum, and a cap on the total weight turns it into the spacing-INDEPENDENT c that familyOfSortedCount consumes, so ymFamilyTension's os_gap is DERIVED from the measured tension where WilsonInstance.ymFamily and WilsonGauge.ymFamilyGauge both hardwire the spectrum their hcount counts. The witness read is the circle shape rho(d) = r^circLag(d) and its aperture comes from aperture_factor_tendsto_zero -- no threshold is named anywhere. A1_YM (ymModelAt N) IS confinement_of_bounded_substrate's per-N conclusion definitionally; it is NOT A1_YM ymModel, because that conclusion is eventual in the aperture with a threshold set by the existentially supplied B, so the pinned nCorrYM cannot be placed above it. Non-degenerate: J infinite, Na -> infinity, exactly one mode resolved at every spacing, c positive and at least the count, the read not the flat default. Q non-vanishing is NOT proved -- a pre-existing gap shared by both older families, needing a positivity lemma for LatticeGauge.System.expect under probHaar. The measure side is foundational-only; wilson_reflection_positive_at enters only through the gap side at muYMAt.
import MassGap.Substrate  -- what reflection positivity CANNOT give, proved. ym_mass_gap_of_substrate needs one hypothesis, exists B, forall N beta, d2At N beta <= B. circ_moment_le_quarter_sq bounds the circle second moment of ANY Moment.Read by (N+1)^2/4 unconditionally, and antipodeRead_moment_eq_quarter_sq ATTAINS it, so 1/4 is the best constant the axiom supports -- while substrateRatio must sit under (1-3^(-1/4))/8 = 0.030 to be useful, so the trivial bound is 8.3x on the WRONG side and grows without bound (quarter_bound_grows_without_bound). substrate_bound_needs_more_than_positivity states the closure as one theorem. The spectral-form escape is closed too: flatSpectral is a genuine PeriodicSpectralForm with lam = 1 (contractivity is not a gap), and flatRead_exceeds_ceiling puts it 2.78x over. AND bounded_moment_does_not_give_geometric_decay proves the two residuals are NOT one: tailRead has circle moment 1/(k+1) <= 1 at every aperture yet no geometric C*r^d bounds it, so a decay RATE is strictly stronger than the flagship needs -- which matters because asymptotic freedom denies a rate uniform in beta while a Cesaro moment bound survives it. Foundational only except the two statements about the Wilson read, which carry exactly the flagship's own footprint.
import MassGap.ReflectPositive  -- the RP axiom REDUCED to Osterwalder-Seiler proper, and the axiom's own framing shown defective. corrHyper_eq_pairing proves the lag displacement IS the tree's reflection: corrHyper equals the Gibbs pairing of the centred plaquette-energy observable with its own reflConf image, via hol_reflConf and expect_reflect_invariant. corrClay_rp_of then derives the axiom's exact conjunction from (1) PlaqReflPositive, textbook Osterwalder-Seiler narrowed to ONE observable with its locality side condition machine-checked (plaq_link_ne_refl: every link of the base plaquette sits at lag-coordinate 0 and its mirror at c, so the two halves read disjoint links at nonzero lag), and (2) 0 < corrClay ... 0, which is positivity of the plaquette energy's VARIANCE and is NOT reflection positivity -- the identically-zero correlation satisfies every pairing inequality and fails it. The axiom bundles two facts of different provenance and should be split. pairing_nonpos_of_odd proves RP cannot be stated observable-free: oddObs has pairing -<O^2> <= 0, so any all-observables form is FALSE. Zero of the 60 carriers are freed: this is a conditional theorem, the axiom is untouched.
import MassGap.CubeBranch  -- the entropy floor RAISED above (1/4) log 3, by counting a strictly richer subfamily of the same closed surfaces. Floor+CubeArea count DIRECTED CUBE-PATHS: 3^k of them, each bounding a distinct closed surface of area exactly 4k+6, giving kappa_0 >= (1/4) log 3 = 0.2746531. Paths are not the only surfaces of that area and kappa_0 is a limsup over ALL closed surfaces, so a richer subfamily bounds the SAME quantity from below by more. The family here is a path (the SPINE) of (d+1)k+1 steps carrying ONE extra cube per block of d+1 steps, at one of d positions in the block, on an axis FORCED to avoid both the spine direction at its own index and the next one. Every cube but the origin then has exactly one face-neighbour below it, so the configuration is a TREE and the SAME double count CubeArea.boundary_card_of_shared makes -- already stated there for an arbitrary Finset Cube -- gives |dC| = 6n - 2(n-1) = 4n+2, the path's own area law at n = k+1. eq_of_boundaryFaces_eq frees CubeArea's surface-injectivity from the path entirely: mem_boundaryFaces_iff_floor decides membership on the floor and mem_boundaryFaces_iff_xor propagates it, so ANY two configurations with the same boundary are equal and any family is counted by its surfaces as soon as it is counted by its cubes. branched_surfaces_count_and_area: 3^((d+1)k+1) * d^k distinct surfaces, each of area exactly 4((d+2)k+2)+2. The density is ((d+1)log3 + log d)/(4(d+2)), which beats (1/4)log3 exactly when log d > log 3, i.e. d > 3 -- and d = 3 reproduces the path floor EXACTLY (3^(d+1)*d = 3^(d+2) over the same area), which is the negative control. Best at d = 10: kappa_0 >= (11 log 3 + log 10)/48 = 0.2997358. Closedness transports free (CubeClosed.edge_parity_all is already general); CONNECTEDNESS of the new boundaries is NOT proved here -- CubeConnected's descent is written for the one-cube-per-layer path -- so this raises the counted floor and does not yet replace CubeConnected's input to VortexFamily. Checked numerically by certify/floor_branch_family.py, negative controls included. Foundational only.
